## Why This Is Asked
Testing idempotent payment flows under bank failures is critical for reliability and user trust.

## Key Concepts
- Idempotency and Idempotency-Key semantics
- End-to-end testing with external banks
- Race conditions and concurrency
- Failure injection and retry/backoff strategies
- Data reconciliation and compensation patterns

## Code Example
```javascript
// Minimal skeleton for an idempotent charge test
async function testIdempotentCharge(client, amount, key) {
  const r1 = await client.post('/payments/charge', { amount }, { headers: { 'Idempotency-Key': key } })
  const r2 = await client.post('/payments/charge', { amount }, { headers: { 'Idempotency-Key': key } })
  if (r1.chargeId !== r2.chargeId) throw new Error('Idempotency violated')
  if (r2.status !== 'succeeded') throw new Error('Unexpected status')
}
```

